        "arguments": "{\"thought\": \"Now I will add the **Communication Interface** (Isolated and Direct).\\n\\n**Isolated Interface (U2 - ISO7342):**\\n*   **Power:**\\n    *   Side 1 (BMS side): `VCC1` (Pin 1) -> `CVDD` via J18.\\n    *   Side 2 (MCU side): `VCC2` (Pin 16) -> `USB2ANY_3.3V`.\\n    *   Decoupling: C58 on `CVDD_CO` (Side 1), C57 on `USB2ANY_3.3V` (Side 2).\\n    *   GNDs: `GND11`/`GND12` -> `CVSS` (GND). `GND21`/`GND22` -> `USB2ANY_GND` (Isolated GND).\\n    *   Wait, SCUD says \\\"U2 Isolated side powered by USB2ANY_3.3V. BMS side powered by CVDD via J18.\\\"\\n    *   J18 connects `CVDD` to `CVDD_CO`.\\n    *   So U2.VCC1 is connected to `CVDD_CO`.\\n    *   C58 is on `CVDD_CO`.\\n    *   C57 is on `USB2ANY_3.3V`.\\n\\n*   **Signal Flow:**\\n    *   **TX (MCU -> BMS):**\\n        *   `USB2ANY_TX_3.3` (J17-7) -> U2.INB (Pin 4).\\n        *   U2.OUTB (Pin 13) -> `RX_CO`.\\n        *   `RX_CO` -> J21 -> `RX` (U1-52).\\n    *   **RX (BMS -> MCU):**\\n        *   `TX` (U1-53) -> U2.INC (Pin 12).\\n        *   U2.OUTC (Pin 5) -> `USB2ANY_RX_3.3` (J17-8).\\n    *   **Fault (BMS -> MCU):**\\n        *   `NFAULT` (U1-62) -> J2 -> `NF_J`.\\n        *   `NF_J` -> U2.IND (Pin 11).\\n        *   U2.OUTD (Pin 6) -> `NFAULT_C` (J17-3).\\n    *   **Unused/Other:**\\n        *   U2.INA (Pin 3) -> R123 -> GND (SCUD says \\\"tied to GND via R123\\\").\\n        *   U2.OUTA (Pin 14) -> Unconnected.\\n        *   Enables: EN1 (Pin 7), EN2 (Pin 10). Usually pulled high or tied to VCC. SCUD doesn't specify. I'll assume tied to VCC or internal pullup. Let's check if there are resistors.\\n        *   SCUD doesn't mention EN pins. I'll leave them floating if internal pullup, or tie to VCC. Standard is tie to VCC. I'll leave them for now or check if I missed something.\\n        *   Wait, SCUD says \\\"U2 INA (Pin 3) being tied to GND via R123\\\".\\n        *   I need to add R123.\\n\\n**Direct Interface (J3, J1):**\\n*   J3 (6-pin header, but only 4 used? SCUD says \\\"