ered by CVDD\\\". CVDD is U1 regulator.\\n    *   \\\"Isolated side powered by USB2ANY\\\".\\n    *   If Side 1 (Pins 1-8) is powered by VCC1.\\n    *   If Side 2 (Pins 9-16) is powered by VCC2.\\n    *   Which side is which?\\n    *   SCUD: \\\"TX (MCU -> BMS): USB2ANY_TX_3.3 (J17-7) -> U2 (INB->OUTB) -> RX_CO\\\".\\n    *   If INB is Pin 4 (Side 1), then Side 1 is MCU.\\n    *   If OUTB is Pin 13 (Side 2), then Side 2 is BMS.\\n    *   Let's check power again.\\n    *   \\\"BMS side powered by CVDD\\\".\\n    *   If Side 2 is BMS, then VCC2 (Pin 16) should be CVDD.\\n    *   \\\"U2 Isolated side powered by USB2ANY_3.3V\\\".\\n    *   If Side 1 is MCU, then VCC1 (Pin 1) should be USB2ANY_3.3V.\\n    *   Let's verify with \\\"RX (BMS -> MCU): TX (U1-53) -> U2 (INC->OUTC) -> USB2ANY_RX_3.3\\\".\\n    *   BMS TX -> INC. MCU RX <- OUTC.\\n    *   If BMS is Side 2, INC should be on Side 2.\\n    *   Mapping: INC is Pin 12 (Side 2). Correct.\\n    *   OUTC is Pin 5 (Side 1). Correct.\\n    *   So:\\n        *   **Side 1 (Pins 1-8) = MCU / Isolated Side.** Power: `USB2ANY_3.3V`. GND: `USB2ANY_GND`.\\n        *   **Side 2 (Pins 9-16) = BMS / High Voltage Side.** Power: `CVDD_CO`. GND: `GND` (System GND).\\n    *   Wait, SCUD says \\\"U2 Isolated side powered by USB2ANY_3.3V. BMS side powered by CVDD via J18.\\\"\\n    *   This matches.\\n    *   So:\\n        *   VCC1 (Pin 1) -> `USB2ANY_3.3V`.\\n        *   GND1 (Pin 2, 8) -> `USB2ANY_GND`.\\n        *   VCC2 (Pin 16) -> `CVDD_CO`.\\n        *   GND2 (Pin 9, 15) -> `GND`.\\n\\n    *   **Connections:**\\n        *   **MCU -> BMS (TX):**\\n            *   J17-7 (`USB2ANY_TX_3.3`) -> U2.INB (Pin 4).\\n            *   U2.OUTB (Pin 13) -> `RX_CO`.\\n            *   `RX_CO` -> J21 -> `RX`.\\n        *   **BMS -> MCU (RX):**\\n            *   U1.TX -> U2.INC (Pin 12).\\n            *   U2.OUTC (Pin 5) -> `USB2ANY_RX_3.3` (J17-8).\\n        *   **BMS -> MCU (Fault):**\\n            *   U1.NFAULT -> J2 -> `NF_J`.\\n            *  