n    *   SCUD: \"Channel 1... GPIO1_C connects to J4 Pin 2. Thus, the BMS pin GPIO1 measures...\"\n    *   So J4 Pin 2 is `GPIO1_C`. J4 Pin 1 is likely `GPIO1` (U1 Pin 61).\n    *   Wait, \"GPIO1 connects directly to GPIOx_R when the jumper is placed.\"\n    *   For Channel 1: `GPIO1_R` -> Filter -> `GPIO1_C` -> J4.2 -> Jumper -> J4.1 -> `GPIO1`.\n    *   For Channels 2-8: `GPIOx_R` -> J4.even -> Jumper -> J4.odd -> `GPIOx`.\n    *   I'll assume J4 Odd pins = U1 GPIOs, J4 Even pins = Divider points.\n    *   Mapping:\n        *   GPIO1: J4.1 - J4.2 (Signal `GPIO1_C`)\n        *   GPIO2: J4.3 - J4.4 (Signal `GPIO2_R`)\n        *   ...\n        *   GPIO8: J4.15 - J4.16 (Signal `GPIO8_R`)\n\n**GPIO1 Filter:**\n*   `GPIO1_R` -> R128 (1k) -> `GPIO1_C`.\n*   `GPIO1_R` -> C60 (1uF) -> `GND`.\n*   `GPIO1_R` -> D3 (Cathode) -> `GND`? SCUD says \"D3: 24V Dual Zener/TVS\". Usually Cathode to Signal, Anode to GND. Or Bidirectional.\n*   Mapping for `BZX84C24`: pin1=Anode, pin2=pin2, pin3=Cathode.\n*   Dual Zener usually has common anode or cathode. SOT-23.\n*   If it's a dual series zener (bidirectional), it might be Pin 1 and 2 to lines, Pin 3 to GND? Or Pin 3 is common.\n*   SCUD says \"D3: 24V Dual Zener/TVS Diode\".\n*   I'll check `subckt_gpios.png` if I can.\n*   If not, I'll assume standard protection: Signal -> D3 -> GND.\n*   I'll use `BZX84C24` pin 1 and 3? Or just 1 and 2?\n*   Let's assume Pin 3 (Cathode) to Signal, Pin 1 (Anode) to GND.\n\n**Aux Measurement:**\n*   `BBP` (U1-64) and `BBN` (U1-63).\n*   Path 2 (Active): `SRP_S` -> `BBP`, `SRN_S` -> `BBN`.\n*   Path 1 (DNP): `BBP_CELL` -> R9 -> `BBP`. `BBN_CELL` -> R12 -> `BBN`.\n*   I'll define nets `SRP_S`, `SRN_S`, `BBP_CELL`, `BBN_CELL`.\n*   Connect `SRP_S` to `BBP`.\n*   Connect `SRN_S` to `BBN`.\n*   Add R9, R12, C10 (DNP/Active?). SCUD says Path 1 is DNP.\n*   \"R9, R12 (402\u03a9)... Currently DNP.\"\n*   \"C10 (0.47uF)...\"\n*   I'll add them but maybe not connect them to the main nets if they are DNP? No, I should wire them as if the PCB exists.\n*   So: `BBP_CELL` -> R9 -> `BBP`. `BBN_CELL` -> R12 -> `BBN`.\n*   C10 between `BBP` and `BBN`? Or before resistors? \"Differential RC filter formed by R9/R12 and C10\". Usually C is after R. So C10 between `BBP` and `BBN`.\n*   Path 2: \"Directly wired to BBP/BBN\".\n*   So `SRP_S` -> `BBP`. `SRN_S` -> `BBN`.\n\n**LED:**\n*   `PWR` -> R121 (1k) -> J6.1 -> J6.2 -> D1 (Anode) -> D1 (Cathode) -> `GND`.\n*   Wait, SCUD says \"Green LED D1 with R121 (1.0k) and Jumper J6\".\n*   Usually LED is on low voltage side? No, \"Power Indicator\".\n*   If it's on `PWR` (High Voltage), 1k is too small for HV (e.g. 48V).\n*   Maybe it's on `LDOIN` or `CVDD`?\n*   SCUD says \"Indicator: Green LED D1...\". Doesn't explicitly say which rail.\n*   But \"NPN Supply... Input Path: PWR...\".\n*   Let's check `subckt_test_points.png` or `subckt_pow_supply.png`.\n*   Actually, if it's a \"High-cell-count BMS\", PWR is HV.\n*   Maybe it's on `CVDD` (5V) or `DVDD`?\n*   I'll assume `CVDD` or `LDOIN`.\n*   Let's look at the text again. \"Indicator: Green LED D1...\".\n*   I'll check `subckt_pow_supply.png` again.\n\nI'll delete the file and start the full build including Pass 3.\n\n**Full Build Plan:**\n1.  Imports.\n2.  Board.\n3.  Nets (Power, Comms, Aux, GPIOs).\n4.  U1 Instantiation & Power/Decoupling.\n5.  NPN Supply.\n6.  Isolator U2 & Comms Connectors.\n7.  Cell Inputs (Direct & Config Resistors).\n8.  Thermistors & GPIO Interface.\n9.  Aux Inputs.\n10. LED.\n\n**LED Rail:** I'll guess `CVDD` (5V) or `LDOIN`. 1k resistor on 5V gives 3mA (dim) or 5mA. On 48V it would burn. So it must be a low voltage rail. `CVDD` is a good candidate.\n\n**Cell Inputs:**\nI need to add `VC0`..`VC16` and `CB0`..`CB16` nets.\nAnd connect them to U1.\nAnd add the config resistors.\n\n**Thermistors:**\nI need to add 8x `resistor` (10k), 8x `NCP18XH103F03RB`.\nAnd J5.\nAnd J4.\nAnd the GPIO1 filter.\n\n**Let's go.**\n\nI'll delete the file first.",
